<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yafa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yafa are a tribal confederation of the highlands north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. In the early 18th century they threw off the rule of the Qasimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a> and formed the Upper and Lower Yafa sultanates. Yafa'i men served widely as soldiers, in the Hadramawt and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and Yafa'i families founded the Kasadi and Qu'aiti dynasties.</p></div>
